  "name": "docker-sandboxes-kits",
  "description": "Use this skill when authoring, verifying, publishing, or composing a Docker Sandboxes kit, even if the user just says they want to \"add a tool to a sandbox agent\", \"package a CLI or agent as a kit\", \"publish a kit to a registry\", or \"give a mixin its own credentials and network access\". Covers the v3 kit descriptor (`# syntax=docker/sandbox-kit:3`, `kind: workload` or `mixin`, typed capabilities, provides/requires, content recipes), building with docker buildx, checking with kit-tck and `sbx kit inspect`, composing onto a workload, and publishing and signing. Legacy v2 `spec.yaml` kits are not covered; `sbx kit validate` is not a substitute for kit-tck conformance and runtime checks.",
